  "note": "decode: none clock: 2026-11-06T16:46:23.000Z\nLocale and time zone are pinned by scripts/oracle/l1/core/renderer/locale.ts, loaded before the app module: process.env.TZ = 'UTC', and Intl.RelativeTimeFormat, Date.prototype.toLocaleString and String.prototype.localeCompare get 'en-US' when the app passes undefined (toLocaleString also gets timeZone 'UTC'), as the UI captures run. Node's own ICU (Node 24.13.1, ICU 78.2, CLDR 48.0) produces the text.\nThe relative-time formatter is built once, at module load, with numeric 'auto' (yesterday, last week).\nEvery case passes now (arg1) as a Date except the two default-now cases, which leave it out so the function reads new Date(): the clock is on for those, and their iso is placed days or hours from 2026-11-06T16:46:23.000Z so the seconds the oracle clock runs on cannot change the answer.\narg0 goes through new Date(iso), so the parse cases record V8 Date.parse leniency; a Rust port must accept and refuse exactly the same strings.\ngap: src/renderer/src/lib/time.ts:13:57 default parameter, not measured by V8; the two default-now cases run it.",
